{"name":"Spice Bazaar","hex":"#86613f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aromatic or pungent plant matter (usually dried) used to season or flavor food.","The quality of being spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add spice or spices to; season.","To spice up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice"},{"term":"bazaar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marketplace, particularly in the Middle East and South Asia, and often covered with shops and stalls.","A shop selling articles that are either exotic or eclectic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bazaar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spice Bazaar","blocks":[{"text":"The Spice Bazaar in Istanbul, Turkey, is one of the largest bazaars in the city. Located in the Eminönü quarter of the Fatih district, it is the most famous covered shopping complex after the Grand Bazaar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Spice_Bazaar_Istanbul_Feb_2020%2C_img_2.jpg/330px-Spice_Bazaar_Istanbul_Feb_2020%2C_img_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice_Bazaar"},{"title":"Spice Bazaar (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"The Spice Bazaar restaurants comprise multiple Desi and Continental cuisine restaurants in Lahore, Punjab, Pakistan."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice_Bazaar_(restaurant)"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice"},{"title":"Bazaar","blocks":[{"text":"A bazaar or souk is a marketplace consisting of multiple small stalls or shops, especially in West Asia, North Africa, the Balkans, Central Asia, and South Asia. They are traditionally located in vaulted or covered streets that have doors on each end and served as a city's central marketplace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Turkey_%2868742801%29.jpeg/330px-Turkey_%2868742801%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bazaar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG/120px-Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG/250px-Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG/120px-Istanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIstanbul_Misir_carsisi.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/20131204_Istanbul_237.jpg/120px-20131204_Istanbul_237.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/20131204_Istanbul_237.jpg/250px-20131204_Istanbul_237.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https